<title>UK: BZW Endowment Fund II offering oversubscribed.</title>
<headline>BZW Endowment Fund II offering oversubscribed.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>An offering of 11.5 million shares by BZW Endowment Fund II at one pound each was 1.5 times oversubscribed and an additional 13.5 million were placed with investors, Barclays Global Investors Ltd said in a statement.</p>
<p>Dealing in partly paid shares, the first instalment is 50 pence, will start on December 18.</p>
<p>&quot;We do have a an advantage over most other endowment funds as we will be looking for policies maturing in each of the five years, rather than one single year, at the end of the fund's life,&quot; said Paul Seymour the fund's chairman.</p>
<p>-- David Chance London Newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
